 "note": [
  "Scripture source: the Indian Revised Version (IRV Hindi, CC BY-SA 4.0), fetched as USX from the ebible mirror (gracious-tech/fetch_collection, bibles/hin_irv/usx), all 66 books. Every mined span was sliced from that text by script, never typed; translators also had an English-phrase search over the whole Bible keyed to the same verse ids, since Spurgeon quotes almost entirely without citations.",
  "Derived by measurement: a row is mined only when the translator reported the quotation verbatim AND the measurement confirms it — a 6+ character quoted segment in that block, or an 8+ character phrase anywhere in the chapter (readings often quote a verse in their <h3> heading), is a byte substring of the cited IRV verse. adapted (person/grammar changed), self (IRV differs) and 9 verbatim claims the measurement could not confirm are self_rendered. Unquoted echoes are not recorded.",
  "KJV/IRV divergences an editor should see: Job 13:15 IRV reads 'I have no hope' — Spurgeon's 'yet will I trust in him' is self-rendered, identically in ch02 and ch03; Job 42:10 no 'turned the captivity'; Luke 15:2 'मिलता है' where the reading turns on 'receiveth'; Isa 26:4 'सनातन चट्टान' for 'everlasting strength'; Song 1:4 no 'the upright'; Song 8:6 no 'mightier than the grave' (the second half of that quotation in ch07 is the translator's own wording inside the quotation marks — a reviewer should look); 1 Cor 15:55 no 'grave'; Luke 2:14 no 'good will towards men'; Rom 5:1 'let us have peace'; Ps 110:3 dew of 'thy young men'; Phil 3:20 स्वदेश (citizenship) where the KJV's 'conversation' means conduct; Rev 3:4 no 'even' or 'names'; Isa 53:3 रोग where Spurgeon plays on 'grief'.",
  "IRV typos: copied byte-for-byte in 2 Cor 1:5 and Eccl 7:6 (the latter only up to the typo, the rest supplied). One translator instead corrected Ps 92:5 'बड़े है' to 'बड़े हैं' (ch15) — so that row is not verbatim IRV.",
  "Conventions: straight double quotes mirror the English exactly per chapter (this book's source is straight-quoted throughout; the shipped hi books mirror their sources); chapter titles pinned up front; supplication विनती (IRV spelling; one बिनती normalised), 'Beloved' प्रियो; Bunyan's pilgrims rendered once and reused — अल्प-विश्वास (Little-faith), महा-विश्वास (Great-faith), श्री महा-हृदय (Mr. Great-heart), सत्य-के-लिये-वीर (Valiant-for-truth).",
  "ENGLISH SOURCE items found and NOT repaired (the Hindi mirrors them): hymn stanzas sit as loose text between </p> and <p> in ch03, ch06, ch08, ch10, ch13, ch14 and ch16 (untagged in the fixture); ch14 'rain or heaven' for 'rain of heaven'; ch04 'ones' self'; ch19's first reading is about trials, not the Holy Spirit (compiler's placement); Spurgeon's own slips kept as written: 'his father's flock' for Moses (father-in-law's, ch18), Isaiah credited with Ps 27:14 (ch01), David with Ps 87:7 (ch10), the people for Caleb's Num 13:30 (ch14), 'every man a shekel' (half a shekel, ch02), 'word of testimony' for 2 Pet 1:19 (ch12)."
